<speak>
From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your daily briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17022026</say-as>.
<break time="1s"/>
In politics.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Bangladesh's</emphasis> Nobel laureate <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="muˈhɑməd ˈjuːnus">Muhammad Yunus</phoneme> stepped down as interim leader after Bangladesh National Party chairman <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɑˈriːk rɑhˈmɑn">Tarique Rahman</phoneme> won <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">209</say-as> of <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">297</say-as> parliamentary seats. <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈjuːnus">Yunus</phoneme> urged the country to safeguard democracy and free speech in his farewell broadcast.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Iran's</emphasis> Foreign Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔæbˈbɑːs ɑːɾɑɣˈt͡ʃi">Abbas Araqchi</phoneme> arrived in Geneva for a second round of indirect nuclear talks with the United States, mediated by <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="oʊˈmɑːn">Oman</phoneme>. The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps began drills in the Strait of Hormuz, which carries twenty percent of the world's traded oil, one day after a US carrier group deployed to the Persian Gulf.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Lebanon</emphasis> announced a four-month timeline to dismantle <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɛzboˈlɑ">Hezbollah's</phoneme> arsenals between the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="lɪˈtɑːni">Litani</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɑːˈwɑːli">Awali</phoneme> rivers, extending disarmament forty kilometers north of the ceasefire zone. <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɛzboˈlɑ">Hezbollah's</phoneme> chief called the plan a grave sin, and the group has not said whether it will comply.
<break time="900ms"/>
In conflict and security.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Ukraine's</emphasis> forces retook <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">201</say-as> square kilometers east of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zɑpɔˈrɪʒʒjɑ">Zaporizhzhia</phoneme> in five days, their fastest advance since the June <say-as interpret-as="date" format="y">2023</say-as> counteroffensive. The gain gives <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkiːjiw">Kyiv</phoneme> rare battlefield momentum days before Geneva talks open.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Sudan's</emphasis> army drones killed <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">28</say-as> people at a market in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="soʊˈdɑːri">Sodari</phoneme>, North <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɔrˈdoʊfɑn">Kordofan</phoneme>, with another <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">26</say-as> dead in a midnight strike on a displacement shelter housing families. The aerial campaign deepens a three-year war that has killed at least <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">40000</say-as> and displaced twelve million people.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Pakistan</emphasis> saw suicide bombers strike three districts near the Afghan border, killing <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">14</say-as> people including eight police and paramilitary troops. No group has claimed responsibility, but similar attacks have targeted security forces in the region for months.
<break time="900ms"/>
On the economy.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Argentina's</emphasis> Confederación General del Trabajo called a twenty-four-hour general strike for Thursday, when the lower house votes on reforms allowing twelve-hour workdays and reduced severance. This marks the fourth general strike under President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="miˈlei">Milei</phoneme> as he pushes final approval before his March address.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Japan's</emphasis> economy grew just zero point one percent last quarter, reversing a prior contraction but falling far short of the one point six percent economists expected. The underwhelming rebound pressures the Bank of Japan to delay further interest rate increases as the world's fourth-largest economy stalls.
<break time="900ms"/>
In technology.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">China's</emphasis> <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɑliˈbɑbɑ">Alibaba</phoneme> launched <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="t͡ʃwɛn">Qwen</phoneme>-three point five, a <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">397</say-as> billion parameter model offering multimodal support for text, images, and video. The model matches OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google DeepMind while costing sixty percent less to run, accelerating an open-source strategy that undercuts the closed, subscription-based approach of United States competitors.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Ireland's</emphasis> Data Protection Commission opened a European Union privacy investigation into how X's chatbot <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɡrɑk">Grok</phoneme> processed personal data to create artificial intelligence-generated images that digitally undressed real people. French prosecutors raided X's Paris offices this month, and British regulators launched their own probes.
<break time="1s"/>
That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.
</speak>